  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a substantive denial that requires an appeal to overturn; resubmission is prohibited by the payer's duplicate claim rules. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is a valid and often effective next step to challenge the medical necessity of the bundling determination. The previous P2P request likely did not resolve the issue or was not completed, so re-initiating or ensuring the P2P is active is the correct procedural move before filing a formal appeal.",
